<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-Stora H1 profit falls 24 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Stora H1 profit falls 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group Stora released on Tuesday its results for the six months ending June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  1,224 vs  1,610</p>
<p> Sales					22,023 vs 24,041</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 2.50 vs 3.30</p>
<p> Operating costs			  18,380 vs 20,402</p>
<p> Nonrecurring items	    CHARGE    150 vs     71 CREDIT</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,882 vs  1,827</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,611 vs  1,883</p>
<p> Net financial items			 387 vs    273</p>
<p> Minorities				     12 vs     11</p>
<p> Tax					     404 vs    539</p>
<p> Net profit				    808 vs  1,060</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll found the market expected a profit after financial items of 1.13 billion crowns for the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
